 "keywords": ["AI coding assistant security", "malicious VS Code extension", "Cursor extension backdoor", "LLMjacking", "AI API key security", "developer endpoint security", "software supply chain UAE", "signed container images", "fractional CTO UAE", "secure SDLC AI"], "faq": [["What happened with the malicious Claude Code extension?", "Cursor reported that tampered versions of the Claude Code extension were listed in its marketplace for a few hours on 29 October 2026. Microsoft's analysis describes a loader that tried to plant an SSH key and open a reverse tunnel. Anthropic said its own systems were not compromised."], ["What is LLMjacking and why does it matter to software companies?", "LLMjacking is the theft and resale of access to AI models, usually through stolen API keys or cloud credentials. Keys stored in developer platforms, laptops or CI systems can be used to run large volumes of model calls at the victim's expense."], ["Do we need to ban AI coding tools?", "No. The aim is to control what they can reach: approved extensions only, no long-lived secrets on laptops, model access through a gateway with limits, and verified builds before anything reaches a client."]], "related": ["/uae/", "/fractional-cto/", "/ai-architect/"], "citations": [{"title": "Inside a malicious Claude Code-branded extension and its persistent SSH backdoor", "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/10/30/inside-malicious-claude-code-branded-cursor-extension-persistent-ssh-backdoor/", "publisher": "Microsoft Security", "date": "30 Oct 2026"}, {"title": "Security notice: malicious version of Anthropic.claude-code (2.1.312 and 2.1.313) identified in the Cursor VS Code Extension Marketplace", "url": "https://cursor.com/blog/claude-code-extension-security-notice", "publisher": "Cursor", "date": "Oct 2026"}, {"title": "Black October: LLMJacking Wave Exposes AI Infrastructure's Credential Crisis", "url": "https://futurumgroup.com/insights/black-october-llmjacking-wave-expo